ops.body:
reposync implementation workflow wf_b9d6f927-ff6 complete: cc-sync/worktree-snapshot @ 3ea2d6b6fa95 (integration 76e7ece + review fixes 3a59190/113a9b1/3ea2d6b). 16 review findings: 15 fixed, each with a real git/git-lfs/jj regression test that fails on 76e7ece, and 1 rejected.
Fixed:
- assume-unchanged/skip-worktree edits captured via read-only `ls-files -v -s -z`;
- LFS detection no longer depends on filter.lfs config;
- per-commit `check-attr --source` for history pointers;
- LFS added only in merge commits (--diff-merges=combined);
- ReadOnlyGitEnv pins core.hooksPath=/dev/null, core.fsmonitor=false and core.splitIndex=false;
- submodules are statused individually under their own filter overrides;
- the LFS dedup respects the exec bit;
- ErrBusy on type/mode change during read;
- verify/restore fixes.
Rejected: untracked special files (FIFOs/sockets/devices) are not WIP. Git can never track them, and marking them would make every checkout with a dev-server socket permanently incomplete. The coordinator concurs.
The final reposync merge (task #10) reconciles three branches: this one, the delta (D13 Stamp + root fixes + D14, fix pending) and D15 (running). Several fixes overlap: hidden flags, submodule filters, fsmonitor, per-commit LFS attributes. The merge prefers whichever version passed review, then keeps the union of their tests and runs a whole-diff astra review.
